==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|sannr|lang=is}}, {{term|saðr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*sanþaz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsanːʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|anːʏr|lang=is}}

====Adjective====
{{is-adj|sannari|sannastur}}

# [[true]], not a [[lie]], [[authentic]]
#: ''Hún er að [[segja satt|segja '''satt''']].''
#:: She's [[tell the truth|telling the '''truth''']].
#: ''[[w:is:Sönn íslensk sakamál|'''Sönn''' íslensk sakamál]].''
#:: '''Real''' Icelandic criminal cases.
# [[real]], [[genuine]], [[true]]
#: ''Þú ert '''sannur''' vinur.''
#:: You are a '''true''' friend.

